  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian fiscal landscape is experiencing significant scrutiny following diverse reports on public spending and revenue performance. Recent data indicates that the OECD expects the national budget deficit to reach 2.9 percent of GDP by 2026. Simultaneously, various sectors report substantial financial movements, such as tax revenues from online retail platforms and customs receipts. State-owned enterprises face debt levels estimated at 1,604 trillion rupiah, while health sector expenditures have reached 664 trillion rupiah. Further fiscal developments include a budget surplus at Bank Indonesia, significant tax payments from Danantara, and a newly approved operational budget for the central bank for 2027. Additionally, discussions are ongoing regarding the impact of electrical subsidies allocated to data centers, currently reported at 8 trillion rupiah, alongside assessments of the country's mineral and coal resource valuation.",
